WARNING:AVOID_BUG: Avoid crashing the kernel - try using WARN_ON & recovery code rather than BUG() or BUG_ON()
#203: FILE: include/linux/kvm_host.h:1081:
+		BUG();

BUG() or BUG_ON() should be avoided totally.
Use WARN() and WARN_ON() instead, and handle the "impossible"
error condition as gracefully as possible.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/deprecated.html#bug-and-bug-on

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'id < KVM_USER_MEM_SLOTS'
#279: FILE: virt/kvm/kvm_main.c:1245:
+	if ((id < KVM_USER_MEM_SLOTS) && !(mem->flags & KVM_MEM_ALLONES) &&
 	    ((mem->userspace_addr & (PAGE_SIZE - 1)) ||
 	     !access_ok((void __user *)(unsigned long)mem->userspace_addr,
 			mem->memory_size)))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

